(LST-20 — a function whose return type IS declared (`Return a text, "hi".`)
 is statically known, so its result is tagged with that type at the write
 and widens the list only because it differs from the other elements. The
 text reads back as a text, unlike the opaque case in LST-18.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST-20.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   [1, "hi"]
   hi
   number
   text
)
To greeting. Return a text, "hi".

a list called declared is [].
append 1 to declared.
append greeting to declared.
print declared.
print element 2 of declared.
For each item in declared,
  if item is a text, print "text". otherwise if item is a number, print "number". otherwise print "other".
